--- a/docs/aerospace-new-window-or-open.adoc
+++ b/docs/aerospace-new-window-or-open.adoc
@@ -6,9 +6,24 @@
 
 == Synopsis
 
-`aerospace new-window-or-open <app-name>`
+[verse]
+// tag::synopsis[]
+aerospace new-window-or-open <app-name> [--args <app-arguments>...] [position <preset>]
+// end::synopsis[]
 
 == Description
 
 If the target app is already running, open a new window by clicking the first File menu item containing "New".
 If the app is not running, launch it by app name and return.
+
+If `position <preset>` is provided, the newly opened window is placed using the requested floating preset.
+
+Application launch arguments are passed through to `/usr/bin/open`. The first dash-prefixed token starts application arguments; `--args` is `/usr/bin/open`'s delimiter and is not delivered to the application itself. A trailing `position <preset>` is reserved as the final two tokens.
+
+Each distinct set of launch arguments defines a separate application instance profile. A repeat request with the same profile opens a new window in that exact instance; a different profile launches a separate instance via `open -na`. If a live instance has no usable "New Window" menu item, Hyprspace falls back to `open -na` with the same profile.
+
+Example: `aerospace new-window-or-open "Finder" position center`
+
+Example: `aerospace new-window-or-open Helium --args --profile-directory=Default position center`
+
+Example: `aerospace new-window-or-open "Activity Monitor" --args -OpenMainWindow 0`
